body:
ACCEPT-AS-AMENDED — four finite blocker-class repairs. The documentation-only claim ceiling is exact and needs no widening.

1. Scientific conflation: the two-acquisition-run ClockRepair target cannot be named `edition`. The accepted B0 decision explicitly says the repaired diagnostic axis is not the film edition playback axis. Replace run A/B -> edition and edition [5,7) with run A/B -> synthetic repaired diagnostic axis and diagnostic gap [5,7). C09 must preserve that name and identity. Any later relation from this diagnostic axis to an edition axis is separate, evidential and receipted; an F0 edition TrackComposition case may coexist in D without turning the acquisition repair into playback truth.

2. Required B0-C cases are missing from the supposedly exact roster. The accepted oracle also requires record dispositions and legacy distinctions, while V1 has owners only C1B/C/D and covers mainly the F0 adapter subset. Add a C1F or explicit legacy-conformance owner and exact controlled cases for:

- absent TranscriptTurn audio;
- nonempty AudioSpan;
- explicit legacy-empty AudioSpan [t,t);
- packet duration zero as unknown, never the legacy empty value;
- an explicit break-marker record with a typed dropped disposition;
- a retained ordinary-record control;
- optional TR present versus missing;
- missing run coordinate;
- an overlapping-record control yielding every lawful occurrence-scoped preimage;
- within-run mapping control versus split/refused cross-break mapping;
- exactly one closed disposition for every synthetic input record, so no silent loss is possible.

These are provider-free rows and do not authorize source access. F0 compatibility remains intact: B/C/D rows are the accepted F0 SyntheticAdapterMutation subset, while the additional rows satisfy the already-ratified B0-C and C1-F contract.

3. Required lawful outcomes are not yet deterministic in the schema. `unestablished/refused` and `set or Ambiguous` allow two scientifically different answers for one expected-data row. Define the tagged expected-outcome family for every tagged input, not only ProjectionQuery. In particular:

- absent anchor evidence is exactly RelationConstructionOutcome.Unestablished(MissingAnchorEvidence), not operational Refused and not a projection result;
- invalid relation construction is a separately typed refusal;
- timestamp missingness remains a timestamp-envelope result, not projection Gap or generic Option;
- unresolved manifest reference has its own typed finalization refusal;
- finite enumerable reverse preimages have one exact occurrence-scoped set-valued expected result;
- add a separate deliberately underdetermined correspondence control whose exact result is Ambiguous.

Split D04 accordingly and name the exact constructor carrying D02 hold and D03 repeat preimages. Every mutation retains its same-mechanism positive controlCaseId. This removes a required-value representability failure and an evidence-versus-refusal conflation.

4. Reproducibility identity: ExpectedDataId currently hashes selected inputs/outcomes/assertions but omits semantic fields that the artifact says matter, including local axis/relation fixtures, caseId, owner, class, controlCaseId, mutation base/change/detecting-court metadata and possibly header fields. Two different courts could therefore share one ExpectedDataId. Define it as the digest of the canonical encoding of the entire semantic artifact payload: semantic header, every local fixture, complete ordered case records, all typed outcomes/assertions, arithmetic bounds/policies and digest/schema versions. Exclude only explicitly nonsemantic receipt metadata.

For later F0 compatibility, either defer OracleRealizationId entirely to F0 V3 or add the exact realized case-set/coverage and F0 request/Intent identity to its formula. A partial realization must not carry the identity or claim of a full ExpectedDataId realization. F0 two-clean-run request/attempt receipts remain separate; B0-C still establishes no execution or runtime fact.

With those exact changes, ACCEPT. The arithmetic controls, reset/gap/non-bridging laws, independent hand recomputation, C1 self-test prohibition, JVM/JS/Native requirement and claim ceiling are otherwise sufficient. No code, source, runtime, provider or implementation authority follows.
